\time sets the time measure for a bar.
It must be included inside a bar definition,
otherwise it will throw an error.
Its syntax is the following:

\time 3/4

The line above will create a 3 quarter measure.
When a time measure is set, it is held for all
bars defined after it, until a new time measure
is set.
For this reason, when setting a new time measure
it should be set at the beginning of the bar,
like the example below.

\bar time-1 {
    \time 3/4
    \inst c'4 cis'8 c' b4
}
